language sdl-mvp1-exercise version 0.1.

contract CommonServiceContract.
invariant DistinctSequenceDomains.
invariant BoundedSubscribers.
invariant DurableFactsRetained.
invariant ServerBoundAuthority.
invariant StableCommandIdentity.
invariant HiddenTruthIsolated.
invariant DomainTruthOwned.
invariant DiagnosticsSurviveStop.
invariant PreserveRepresentationIdentity.
invariant NoPhysicalExecution.
invariant PureLibraries.
invariant GenericUiMechanisms.
invariant UiResponsiveness.
invariant ConservativeQuality.

CommonServiceContract schema "https://github.com/Hans-Einar/ponsse/blob/7589a5811a21ec6bb13979612060ceff0f690df8/MVP1/contracts/proto/mvp1/common/v1/common.proto".
CommonServiceContract specifies "Hello negotiation, server-bound peer identity, one active subscription, typed resume/baseline and source versus delivery sequence are required by all applicable internal service contracts.".
DistinctSequenceDomains specifies "Service session, source event_seq, delivery stream sequence, command_id, domain revision, target delivery sequence and P1000 sequence remain distinct.".
BoundedSubscribers specifies "A slow observer cannot cause unbounded memory or indefinitely block another observer or an authoritative reducer.".
DurableFactsRetained specifies "Command results, accepted activation/config changes and production facts never use latest-wins. Overflow requires explicit failure/recovery.".
ServerBoundAuthority specifies "Overlapping grants are service-controlled and bound to connection identity; a schema, UI action or caller label grants no authority.".
StableCommandIdentity specifies "Same ID/same payload recovers prior lifecycle; conflicting or expired IDs cannot silently execute as retries.".
HiddenTruthIsolated specifies "Simulator truth is confined to simulator-control and simulator diagnostic views, never normal Target/Machine/Bucking inputs.".
DomainTruthOwned specifies "Machine owns machine/calibration truth; Bucking owns forestry/APT/economics/production unless an explicit ownership migration is adopted.".
DiagnosticsSurviveStop specifies "GlobalStop halts invalidated automation and normal queued intents; observation and evidence collection remain alive.".
PreserveRepresentationIdentity specifies "Presentation replacement preserves semantic instances, domain subscriptions, in-flight command correlation and domain drafts.".
NoPhysicalExecution specifies "This exercise permits offline/simulated design evaluation only; live serial output and actuation are disabled.".
PureLibraries specifies "TaperModels, BuckingCore and StanfordClassic contain no network, UI or service scheduling authority.".
GenericUiMechanisms specifies "UIRuntime and BoxUI generic mechanisms contain no Ponsse business algorithms, P1000 decoder or StanForD parser.".
UiResponsiveness specifies "Realtime values and durable outcomes progress while bulk schema/matrix/profile work is pending; precise budgets remain declared gaps.".
ConservativeQuality specifies "Unknown, unavailable, stale, invalid and pending remain distinguishable from legitimate zero.".
